“Commercial Use” means use of the Software primarily for commercial advantage, monetary compensation, revenue generation, or the operation, development, support, or delivery of a commercial business, product, service, or infrastructure.

Commercial Use includes, without limitation:

(a) selling, licensing, sublicensing, leasing, or renting the Software or a Derivative Work;

(b) incorporating the Software into a commercial product or service;

(c) using the Software to provide a paid or revenue-generating service;

(d) offering the Software through a SaaS, cloud, hosted, managed, or infrastructure service;

(e) using the Software to operate infrastructure or functionality provided to paying customers;

(f) using the Software to develop or operate a competing commercial product or service;

(g) commercially distributing modified versions of the Software;

(h) creating a proprietary commercial product substantially incorporating protected portions of the Software; or

(i) otherwise commercially exploiting protected portions of the Software.

Commercial Use does not include merely viewing publicly available source code or publicly available documentation.

3.5 “Derivative Work”

“Derivative Work” means a work based upon, incorporating, modifying, adapting, translating, transforming, or otherwise reproducing protected portions of the Software in a manner that constitutes a derivative work under applicable copyright law.

A work independently created without copying protected expression from the Software is not made a Derivative Work merely because it implements similar ideas, concepts, algorithms, protocols, interfaces, functionality, or general architectural principles.

